    "content": "**Root cause**: In Python's `re` module, `$` matches at the end of a string **or just before a trailing `\\n`**. This caused header values/names ending with `\\n` (like `\"bar\\n\"`, `\"\\n\"`, `\"foo\\n\"`) to pass validation even though they contain injection-unsafe newlines.\n\n**Fix**: Replace `$` with `\\Z` in all four header validation regexes in `_internal_utils.py`. Unlike `$`, `\\Z` only matches at the true end of the string, regardless of trailing newlines."
